格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Clickable file paths in DSH replies: Codex-style inline open, 📂 reveal in file manager, mentioned-files chip list. DSH web plugin (zero-dependency).","id":"gh:1333960393","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-file-mentions","slug":"a903067276-rgb/dsh-file-mentions","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","file-mentions","web-ui"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Clickable file paths in DSH replies: Codex-style inline open, 📂 reveal in file manager, mentioned-fi"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"les chip list. DSH web plugin (zero-dependency)."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-file-mentions 📎"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Clickable file paths in DSH replies** — a DeepSeek Harness (DSH) web plugin with a Codex-style exp"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ble file paths in DSH replies** — a DeepSeek Harness (DSH) web plugin with a Codex-style experience."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"*Unofficial project: independently developed and maintained by a community member, not an official D"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ct: independently developed and maintained by a community member, not an official DeepSeek product.*"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Screenshot"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Inline paths wrapped in backticks (`` `~/...` ``, absolute, relative, or Chinese paths) become\n[该节后续"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ine paths wrapped in backticks (`` `~/...` ``, absolute, relative, or Chinese paths) become\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Where | What | Effect |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Inline path text | click | Open with default app / open directory |\n| folder icon after inline pat"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"h | click | Reveal in file manager |\n| \"📎 mentioned files\" chip | click name | Preview content insid"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"e DSH |\n| folder icon in the chip list | click | Reveal in file manager |\n| Inline URL | click | Bro"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"wser opens it (official autolink) |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Supports `~/` expansion, relative paths (resolved against the session cwd), and absolute\npaths in ma"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"cOS / Linux / Windows forms. Non-existent paths silently do nothing."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Division of labour with the official features (since 2026-10-01)"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"DSH 0.2 already ships several ways to open files. This plugin **only fills the gaps the official bui"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ld leaves** instead of duplicating them:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Scenario | Owner |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| `@` completion for files/folders/sessions in the composer | **official** (`dsh-file-reference` + `"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ui-reference`) |\n| Markdown file links in messages (`x`, with `#L24`) | **official** (opens in the r"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ight sidebar) — this plugin **skips anything inside `<a>`**, so nothing is decorated twice |\n| The s"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"ession-header \"Open In…\" button and the sidebar preview's \"open with default app / show in folder\" |"},{"id":"p15s5","text":" **official** (`dsh-host-open-in-app`) |\n| **Bare paths in backticks** in message text (`` `~/x/y.md"},{"id":"p15s6","text":"` ``, which the official renderer ignores) | **this plugin**: click to open with the system default "},{"id":"p15s7","text":"app |\n| The folder icon next to a bare path (reveal in file manager) and the \"📎 mentioned files\" rai"},{"id":"p15s8","text":"l at the end of a reply | **this plugin** (no official counterpart) |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- DSH web >= 0.1.0-rc.6 (run with `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`)\n- **Version compatibility** (best effo"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"rt — the settings card uses dual-field `key`+`id` registration to satisfy both rc.6 (`id`) and rc.7+"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" (`key`); verified locally on rc.6/rc.8/0.1.1-rc.2/0.1.2-alpha.2/0.1.5-rc.1 (clickable paths + \"ment"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"ioned files\" panel), **not guaranteed on every DSH version**):\n- DSH 0.1.0-rc.6 and newer (incl. 0.1"},{"id":"p17s5","text":".1-rc.1/rc.2 and 0.1.2): try `main` (default).\n- **DSH 0.1.5-rc.1: load-verified** (the plugin is in"},{"id":"p17s6","text":" the client bundle and `/api/file-mentions/check` responds); UI interactions were not eyeballed item"},{"id":"p17s7","text":" by item. ⚠️ 0.1.5 ships a **narrow** built-in \"clickable inline-code paths in the closing reply\" (o"},{"id":"p17s8","text":"nly files written via `write`/`edit`/`present` in that turn — see `dsh-client-ui-deliverables`), whi"},{"id":"p17s9","text":"ch partially overlaps; plain-text/bare paths, cross-turn and historical messages are still handled o"},{"id":"p17s10","text":"nly by this plugin.\n- Conservative fallbacks (the last pre-0.1.1 build): DSH 0.1.0-rc.7/rc.8 → `v1.0"},{"id":"p17s11","text":".8` (`dsh plugin add github:a903067276-rgb/dsh-file-mentions#v1.0.8`); DSH 0.1.0-rc.6 → frozen `rc6-"},{"id":"p17s12","text":"compat` tag (no maintenance).\n- Pure Node stdlib implementation — peer dependencies (`@deepseek-ai/d"},{"id":"p17s13","text":"sh-settings`,\n`@deepseek-ai/schemastery`) are provided by the host\n- Opening files uses the system d"},{"id":"p17s14","text":"efault app / file manager (per-platform command branching)\n- ✅ **DSH 0.1.7 and later — use this rele"},{"id":"p17s15","text":"ase (`v1.2.2`)**: it declares `peerDependencies: {\"@deepseek-ai/dsh\": \"^0.1.7-rc.1 || ^0.2.0-rc.1\"}`"},{"id":"p17s16","text":", so a mismatched host refuses to load it with an explicit reason instead of failing quietly. Settin"},{"id":"p17s17","text":"gs move to the 0.1.7 model (plugin `Config`, live-editable `.volatile()` fields), so changes apply w"},{"id":"p17s18","text":"ithout a restart.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- **Host** (`lib/index.js`): three routes — `/api/file-mentions/check` (existence check),\n`/api/file"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"-mentions/open` (system open, `mode: open/reveal`, per-platform command) and\n`/api/file-mentions/con"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"fig` (whitelist read/write for the settings page). All three routes\nare same-origin guarded. Probe s"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"urface: absolute/`~/` paths are checked only inside the session cwd or\nuser-declared whitelist roots"},{"id":"p19s5","text":" (stored via the official settings service — immediate\neffect, no restart); whitelist roots are prot"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"ected against system disks and symlink\nescapes. Pure Node stdlib; `execFile` avoids shell injection."},{"id":"p19s7","text":"\n- **Client** (`lib/client.js`): a conversationEvents collector extracts paths from each\nreply → pub"},{"id":"p19s8","text":"lishes them to turn data → the tail list filters non-existent paths before\nrendering; inline clicks "},{"id":"p19s9","text":"use a **document-level click delegation** (the official render\nentry is occupied by the official \"de"},{"id":"p19s10","text":"liverables\" plugin, so DOM delegation is the only\nviable path); inline folder-icon buttons are inser"},{"id":"p19s11","text":"ted by a MutationObserver and restored\nautomatically after React re-renders; a settings card (sideba"},{"id":"p19s12","text":"r section + plugin page)\nedits the whitelist. Scanning/decoration is **incremental**: the observer c"},{"id":"p19s13","text":"allback only\nhandles newly-added nodes inside the official message area (`[data-conversation-scroll]"},{"id":"p19s14","text":"`),\neach new text is cheap-screened for path-like characters (no `/`, `~` or `\\` → skipped\nwith zero"},{"id":"p19s15","text":" regex work and zero requests), and existence checks hit only the current\nsession — conversations wi"},{"id":"p19s16","text":"thout paths trigger no scanning at all; sidebars, hover cards,\nmenus and settings are never touched "},{"id":"p19s17","text":"s trigger no scanning at all; sidebars, hover cards,\nmenus and settings are never touched (v1.0.13)."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"See docs/architecture.md."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Compatibility notes"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- Inline clicks rely on backtick-wrapped paths (the agent-output convention, same as\nCodex); **bare "},{"id":"p22s2","text":"paths inside message text are clickable too** (decoration is\nCSS-Highlight only, zero DOM mutation; "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"message area only — sidebars, hover cards,\nmenus and settings are never touched, v1.0.13).\n- The off"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"icial \"produced files\" list and this plugin coexist: official wins when it has\noutput, otherwise thi"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"s plugin shows.\n- Windows / Linux validation via issue or PR is welcome."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
